content.text:
The database login in alloq isn't SAML. The desktop app signs in with Entra ID (OAuth 2.0 with PKCE, see [app/desktop/entra.py](app/desktop/entra.py)) and gives Postgres the user's access token as the password. In knowledgeai-container the Postgres server currently allows only password login, so three parts of the infrastructure need changes. [doc/desktop.md](doc/desktop.md) already lists the needed settings, but the Terraform there doesn't set any of them yet.

## 1. Postgres server (`terraform/modules/database/main.tf`)

Right now the server has no `authentication` block (so only password login works), no Entra admin, and only the `AllowAllAzureServices` firewall rule.

```hcl
resource "azurerm_postgresql_flexible_server" "postgres" {
  # ...existing settings...
  authentication {
    active_directory_auth_enabled = true
    password_auth_enabled         = true # web apps and migrations still use the admin password
    tenant_id                     = var.tenant_id
  }
}

# Needed to create the Entra principals inside Postgres (step 3)
resource "azurerm_postgresql_flexible_server_active_directory_administrator" "entra_admin" {
  server_name         = azurerm_postgresql_flexible_server.postgres.name
  resource_group_name = var.resource_group_name
  tenant_id           = var.tenant_id
  object_id           = var.entra_admin_object_id   # e.g. a "db-admins" group
  principal_name      = var.entra_admin_name
  principal_type      = "Group"
}

# Desktop clients connect from outside Azure: office/VPN egress IPs
resource "azurerm_postgresql_flexible_server_firewall_rule" "clients" {
  for_each         = var.client_ip_ranges # map(object({ start = string, end = string }))
  name             = each.key
  server_id        = azurerm_postgresql_flexible_server.postgres.id
  start_ip_address = each.value.start
  end_ip_address   = each.value.end
}
```

- `password_auth_enabled` must stay `true`. All web apps log in with the admin user and password from the Key Vault `*-db-*` secrets.
- The module needs new variables `tenant_id`, `entra_admin_object_id`, `entra_admin_name` and `client_ip_ranges`. They have to be passed in from `main.tf`, where `var.tenant_id` already exists.
- Check that `terraform plan` shows the `authentication` change as an in-place update of the existing server.

## 2. App registration (`terraform/modules/app-registration/main.tf`)

The desktop app uses the same client ID as the web app (`common-oauth-azure-client-id`). "Allow public client flows" is already on (`fallback_public_client_enabled = true`). Two settings are missing:

```hcl
data "azuread_service_principal" "ossrdbms" {
  display_name = "Azure OSSRDBMS Database"
}

resource "azuread_application" "app_registration" {
  # ...existing settings...

  public_client {
    redirect_uris = ["http://localhost"] # MSAL loopback; Entra accepts any port
  }

  required_resource_access {
    resource_app_id = data.azuread_service_principal.ossrdbms.client_id
    resource_access {
      id   = data.azuread_service_principal.ossrdbms.oauth2_permission_scope_ids["user_impersonation"]
      type = "Scope"
    }
  }
}

# Admin consent, so users don't each get a consent prompt
resource "azuread_service_principal_delegated_permission_grant" "ossrdbms" {
  count                                = var.create_app_registration ? 1 : 0
  service_principal_object_id          = azuread_service_principal.app_service_principal[0].object_id
  resource_service_principal_object_id = data.azuread_service_principal.ossrdbms.object_id
  claim_values                         = ["user_impersonation"]
}
```

- **Check the lookup:** run `az ad sp list --display-name "Azure OSSRDBMS Database"` first. If the tenant has no service principal for it yet, create one with `azuread_service_principal { client_id = ..., use_existing = true }` instead of the data source.
- **Runner permissions:** the account that runs Terraform needs rights to grant admin consent. If it doesn't have them, a tenant admin grants consent once in the portal.
- **Existing registration:** with `create_app_registration = false`, Terraform doesn't manage the registration. Then the redirect URI, the API permission and the consent all have to be set by hand.

## 3. Inside Postgres (SQL, not Terraform)

Postgres roles can't be created with azurerm. Run this once as the Entra admin. The password is a token from `az account get-access-token --resource-type oss-rdbms`.

```sql
-- in database "postgres": one principal for an Entra group (recommended)
SELECT * FROM pgaadauth_create_principal('alloq-desktop', false, false);

-- in the alloq database
CREATE ROLE alloq_app NOLOGIN;
GRANT CONNECT ON DATABASE alloq TO alloq_app;
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA public TO alloq_app;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public TO alloq_app;
GRANT USAGE, SELECT ON ALL SEQUENCES IN SCHEMA public TO alloq_app;
-- tables created by later migrations (they run as the password admin user)
ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES FOR ROLE <pg_admin_username> IN SCHEMA public
  GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON TABLES TO alloq_app;
ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES FOR ROLE <pg_admin_username> IN SCHEMA public
  GRANT USAGE, SELECT ON SEQUENCES TO alloq_app;
GRANT alloq_app TO "alloq-desktop";
```

Then set `db_role: alloq-desktop` in [configuration/config.desktop.yaml](configuration/config.desktop.yaml). Adding a person is then just adding them to the Entra group. The `ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES` lines are not in `doc/desktop.md` yet. Without them, every new migration creates tables the desktop users can't read.

## No changes needed

- **Key Vault:** the desktop build reads `common-oauth-azure-tenant-id`, `common-oauth-azure-client-id`, `alloq-db-host` and `alloq-db-name`. These secrets already exist through `apps.tf` and the managed secrets. The build machine only needs Get access on the vault.
- **Container App and managed identity:** the server side keeps its password login.

## Security risk

Anyone in the group can use their own token to work directly in the alloq database, without the app's admin checks. Keep the group to alloq admins.

If you want, I can add these changes to knowledgeai-container: the module variables, the two `main.tf` changes, a `tftest` case and a script for the SQL step.

